---
import CodeBlock from '@/components/demos/CodeBlock.astro';
import { vibe2prodVersion } from '@/components/demos/kit-stats';
import { ic, pre, card, link } from '@/components/demos/docs-styles';

const verifySteps = [
  { id: 'format', what: 'Oxfmt' },
  { id: 'oxlint', what: 'JavaScript, TypeScript and Astro scripts (Oxlint)' },
  { id: 'lint-astro', what: 'Astro directives, exports, styles and deprecated APIs' },
  { id: 'astro-check', what: 'Types and templates (astro check)' },
  { id: 'fallow', what: 'Dead code, imports, dependencies, complexity, and duplication' },
  { id: 'lint-design', what: 'Design rules: tokens, links, forms, deprecated APIs' },
  { id: 'lint-docs', what: 'Dead paths, version and count drift in docs' },
  { id: 'registry', what: 'Registry matches component files, props, page templates and recipes' },
  { id: 'test', what: 'Script tests (node --test)' },
  { id: 'build', what: 'Production build' },
  {
    id: 'dist',
    what: 'Built HTML, canonical and sitemap checks, image-control names and exact build files',
  },
];
---

<!-- Cleanup -->
<section id="cleanup" class="scroll-mt-32 lg:scroll-mt-20">
  <div class="mb-8">
    <h2 class="text-3xl font-bold mb-2">Demo Cleanup</h2>
    <p class="text-muted-foreground">
      The download is this demo site. <code class={ic}>pnpm run starter:clean</code> removes it in
      one step; the build-site workflow does this right after intake.
    </p>
  </div>
  <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-6">
    <div class={card}>
      <CodeBlock
        class={pre}
        codeClass="text-sm font-mono"
        code={`pnpm run starter:clean --dry-run   # show the plan
pnpm run starter:clean --yes       # remove the demo
pnpm run starter:clean --yes --keep-blog`}
      />
      <p class="text-sm text-muted-foreground mt-3">
        It is one-shot and destructive: it runs only while the <code class={ic}>starter/</code>{' '}
        folder exists; a second run does nothing (it prints "Already cleaned"). Without{' '}
        <code class={ic}>--yes</code> it asks for confirmation.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class={card}>
      <ul class="space-y-2 text-sm text-muted-foreground list-disc pl-5">
        <li>
          <strong class="text-foreground">Removed:</strong> docs and showcase pages, changelog, demo
          templates, login and privacy samples, demo blog posts, screenshots, evals and maintainer
          docs.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong class="text-foreground">Replaced</strong> with starter versions:{' '}
          <code class={ic}>PROJECT.md</code>, <code class={ic}>site.ts</code>,{' '}
          <code class={ic}>site-url.mjs</code>, the home page, <code class={ic}>robots.txt</code>,{' '}
          <code class={ic}>llms.txt</code>.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong class="text-foreground">Kept:</strong> a minimal home page, the 404 page, all
          sections, layouts, scripts and skills; with <code class={ic}>--keep-blog</code> the blog
          system with one draft post.
        </li>
      </ul>
      <p class="text-sm text-muted-foreground mt-3">
        Afterwards, <code class={ic}>pnpm run verify --starter</code> also fails on demo leftovers.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- Verify -->
<section id="verify" class="scroll-mt-32 lg:scroll-mt-20">
  <div class="mb-8">
    <h2 class="text-3xl font-bold mb-2">Verify</h2>
    <p class="text-muted-foreground">
      <code class={ic}>pnpm run verify</code> runs every check in one go, offline and deterministic,
      and ends with <code class={ic}>VERIFY PASSED</code> or a short list of what failed. If a step
      cannot run, it says so instead of passing.
    </p>
    <p class="mt-2 text-muted-foreground">
      Use <code class={ic}>alt=""</code> for decorative images. Image-only links and native buttons
      containing images need an accessible name. Build files must match exact case and Unicode
      spelling; symlinks are rejected.
    </p>
    <p class="mt-2 text-muted-foreground">
      Static image-control naming checks leave uncertain cases unreported. The visibility of{' '}
      <code class={ic}>hidden="until-found"</code> content depends on computed CSS; an internal
      UNKNOWN result does not prove that a control has a name. Review CSS-dependent cases in a
      browser. Provably empty naming sources still produce a finding, including empty or inert
      content inside an until-found subtree. Role fallback lists use the first role recognized by
      Chromium.
    </p>
  </div>
  <div class="grid grid-cols-1 lg:grid-cols-2 gap-6">
    <div class={`${card} overflow-x-auto`}>
      <table class="w-full text-sm">
        <thead>
          <tr class="border-b text-left">
            <th class="pb-2 pr-4 font-medium text-muted-foreground">Step</th>
            <th class="pb-2 font-medium text-muted-foreground">Checks</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody class="divide-y divide-border">
          {verifySteps.map((s) => (
            <tr>
              <td class="py-2 pr-4 font-mono text-xs whitespace-nowrap">{s.id}</td>
              <td class="py-2 text-muted-foreground">{s.what}</td>
            </tr>
          ))}
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    <div class={card}>
      <CodeBlock
        class={pre}
        codeClass="text-sm font-mono"
        code={`pnpm run verify                # everything
pnpm run verify --starter   # + demo leftovers
pnpm run validate              # interim; skips build and built HTML
pnpm run check:fallow          # strict static analysis
pnpm run lint:design           # single checks
pnpm run lint:docs
pnpm run check:registry`}
      />
      <p class="text-sm text-muted-foreground mt-3">
        The fast command prints{' '}
        <code class={ic}>VALIDATE PASSED (build and built-HTML checks skipped)</code>
        or <code class={ic}>VALIDATE FAILED (n)</code>. Finish with full verification.
      </p>
      <p class="text-sm text-muted-foreground mt-3">
        The design rules behind <code class={ic}>lint:design</code> (semantic color tokens only,
        every link and form pointing somewhere real, no <code class={ic}>ViewTransitions</code>,
        ...) are shared with the optional Claude Code hook.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
  <p class="text-sm text-muted-foreground mt-6">
    <code class={ic}>pnpm run test:e2e</code> runs four homepage tests for content, menu, theme and
    skip-link focus. Back/Forward runs as a named step when a same-tab, same-origin HTML navigation
    document target exists, excluding no-content responses and attachments. Otherwise the command
    prints the reason and records only that step as skipped. MinimalLayout homepages skip the three
    shared-header tests outside kit mode.
  </p>
  <p class="text-sm text-muted-foreground mt-3">
    <code class={ic}>pnpm run test:browser-oracle</code> separately compares image-control naming
    fixtures with Chromium's accessibility tree. It checks deterministic naming and the conservative
    treatment of CSS-dependent <code class={ic}>hidden="until-found"</code> fixtures without an
    Astro build. Both browser commands require Chromium (install it once with{' '}
    <code class={ic}>pnpm exec playwright install chromium</code>); offline verification remains a
    separate check.
  </p>
  <p class="text-sm text-muted-foreground mt-3">
    Kit verification checks recognized source links and fenced clone commands in README,
    CONTRIBUTING and <code class={ic}>public/llms.txt</code> against the shared repository identity.
    It covers repository, source ZIP, registry, AGENTS and skills-tree references; unfamiliar link
    types remain unchecked. Findings identify the URL or command to edit, with shared reference
    definitions reported once. Customer documentation is outside these kit-only checks.
  </p>
</section>

<!-- vibe2prod -->
<section id="vibe2prod" class="scroll-mt-32 lg:scroll-mt-20">
  <div class="mb-8">
    <h2 class="text-3xl font-bold mb-2">vibe2prod Audit</h2>
    <p class="text-muted-foreground">
      The{' '}
      <a
        class={link}
        href="https://github.com/holger1411/vibe2prod"
        target="_blank"
        rel="noopener noreferrer"
      >
        vibe2prod
      </a>{' '}
      skill{vibe2prodVersion && ` (${vibe2prodVersion})`} ships in{' '}
      <code class={ic}>.agents/skills/vibe2prod/</code> (MIT, license included). It audits
      performance, accessibility, SEO, HTML, security, assets, robustness, AI-slop artifacts and
      responsiveness and returns a READY / NOT YET / BLOCKED verdict with a 0–100 score.
    </p>
  </div>
  <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-6">
    <div class={card}>
      <h3 class="font-semibold mb-3">Run it</h3>
      <div class="bg-muted/50 border border-border rounded-xl p-4">
        <p class="text-sm italic">"Run the vibe2prod audit on this project."</p>
      </div>
      <p class="text-sm text-muted-foreground mt-3">
        Without a URL it builds the project and audits a local production server (local project
        mode). After your first deploy, run it again against the live URL. The build-site workflow
        runs it in step 7; agents apply technical fixes and propose content changes.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class={card}>
      <h3 class="font-semibold mb-3">Install its tools once</h3>
      <CodeBlock
        class={pre}
        codeClass="text-sm font-mono"
        code={`pnpm run setup:audit --check   # what is missing
pnpm run setup:audit              # install it`}
      />
      <p class="text-sm text-muted-foreground mt-3">
        Installs Lighthouse, the axe CLI, Playwright with Chromium and axe for Playwright (needs
        network). vibe2prod gives no verdict without its tools; it reports exactly which checks were
        skipped.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
